<!--
FCA-001 (external audit of 1.20.37): the PHP 8.4 floor was previously
asserted only in db/install.php, a POST-install hook that runs AFTER
core has already created the plugin's db/install.xml schema - so the
README's and the hook's own former claim of refusing "before anything
is created" was false. This file is the mechanism Moodle actually
evaluates before that point: core_component::get_plugin_list_with_file()
finds it per plugin, and environment_check() (lib/environmentlib.php,
called from admin/environment.php and from the installer's own
environment gate) reports and enforces it before install/upgrade
proceeds. db/install.php keeps its own check as a backstop only - see
the comment there.

The <PLUGIN name="..."> form (rather than <MOODLE version="...">) is the
one lib/environmentlib.php documents for a plugin's own environment.xml:
get_list_of_environment_versions() treats a PLUGIN element as matching
"all" Moodle versions, and environment_verify_plugin() matches it back to
this component by its name attribute alone - a plugin has one current
requirement, not a table of them per Moodle release.

No <FEEDBACK> block: Moodle's own admin/environment.xml frequently omits
it too (see e.g. its most recent MOODLE version's own <PHP> requirement),
because the standard environment report already renders the numeric
current-vs-needed comparison without one. Adding one here would need a
message resolved either from 'admin' (not this plugin's string) or, with
a plugin="mod_selfselectadvanced" attribute, from this plugin's own
lang file WITHOUT the {$a} substitution get_string() needs to fill in
the running PHP version - and this ticket's file territory does not
extend to lang/en/selfselectadvanced.php to add a version-free string
for it.

version.php requires = 2026042001 is repeated here as an attribute for a
human reading this file beside version.php; environment_verify_plugin()
itself does not read it.
-->
<COMPATIBILITY_MATRIX>
  <PLUGIN name="mod_selfselectadvanced" requires="2026042001">
    <PHP version="8.4.0" level="required" />
  </PLUGIN>
</COMPATIBILITY_MATRIX>
